From 0bdd3385f17999a254277391c92c1e03015d0e82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 23:08:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0155 -- wave-59 fix FT=1 onscreen_objects
 use-after-free crash

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/PHASE11-WAVE-59-CONTRACT.md. Wave-59 is
the fix for the wave-58 Phase-7 crash-to-DOS that nx-engine's static
review root-caused. A correctness FIX, not a lever; FIXED_TIMESTEP=1-
only; the FT=0 production default is left byte-identical.

THE BUG (FT=1-only, patch-0153 accumulator): onscreen_objects[] is the
visibility-culled object list. It is BUILT in DrawScene (the wave-56
render half) and READ + dereferenced by the player sim
(PHandleSolidBrickObjects / PHandleSolidMushyObjects, via HandlePlayer,
in the state half). game_tick_normal_state ends with
Objects::CullDeleted() which FREES deleted objects -- the engine's own
comment there warns stale onscreen_objects entries "blow up the
program on the next tick." The wave-57 FT=1 accumulator
(run_tick_fixed) runs the state half N times then DrawScene ONCE: on
catch-up ticks 2..N, HandlePlayer reads an onscreen_objects[] not
rebuilt since the prior render frame, now holding pointers an earlier
catch-up tick's CullDeleted freed -> use-after-free -> the DJGPP page
fault the operator hit while shooting (First Cave / Polar Star) and
walking (Yamashita Farm). FT=0 is 1:1 -- DrawScene rebuilds
onscreen_objects every tick, so the list is never older than the last
CullDeleted; FT=0 has no bug.

THE FIX: a new file-static _build_onscreen_objects_list() -- the
cull-ONLY half of DrawScene's object loop (the same scr_x/scr_y
onscreen test + the same onscreen_objects[]/nOnscreenObjects/
o->onscreen writes), with NO drawing and none of DrawScene's
per-object render bookkeeping. It is drawcall-free (only READS sprite
metadata: drawpoint/w/h) -- safe for the state half that the
accumulator multi-runs (witness-3 verified: zero drawcall tokens).
game_tick_normal_state calls it at the top of the ModeSim block,
BEFORE HandlePlayer -- so every FT=1 catch-up tick reads a freshly
rebuilt list (live objects only); a prior tick's CullDeleted can no
longer leave a freed pointer in it.

FT=1-GATED -- the essential constraint (contract sec.2.1): the call
is `if (fixed_timestep_active()) _build_onscreen_objects_list();`. On
FT=0 the call never fires; DrawScene remains the sole builder and
game_tick_normal_state runs exactly as wave-58 -> FT=0 renders
byte-identical to production (build-qa Gate 1). An UNCONDITIONAL hoist
would make FT=0's HandlePlayer read this-tick's list instead of the
legacy one-frame-stale list -- a production behavior change; the
gating forecloses that.

DrawScene IS LEFT 100% UNTOUCHED. DrawScene is the FT=0 byte-identity-
critical path; restructuring it to share the cull with the new helper
would risk Gate 1 for no FT=0 benefit. The cull math is therefore
DUPLICATED (the helper + DrawScene's loop) by deliberate choice --
both sites carry a "keep in sync" comment. Under FT=1 DrawScene still
rebuilds onscreen_objects at render time; that is harmless-redundant
(nothing reads it between DrawScene and the next state tick's
rebuild).

SECOND COUPLING CLOSED FOR FREE: the wave-59 process-note sweep (the
[NX?-A] audit gap -- "does the state half READ render-half-built
state") found o->onscreen, a per-object bool also written only by
DrawScene's loop and read by ~6 AI routines (ironhead / sand / sym /
labyrinth_m / last_cave) in the state half -- stale under FT=1 (a
behavior desync, not a crash: it is a live-object bool). Because
_build_onscreen_objects_list() sets o->onscreen in the same loop, the
per-logic-tick rebuild closes that desync too, no extra code.

SWEEP -- other couplings (wave-59 findings, no fix here): game.
showmapnametime is decremented in map_draw_map_name (render half) but
read by NO sim/AI code -- a pure render-rate visual wart (the
stage-name overlay lingers under FT=1), not a sim coupling, benign.
textbox.Tick() IS a render-rate-advanced / TSC-sim-polled coupling,
but TextBox::Tick() is not drawcall-free (it ends with Draw()), so
fixing it needs a TextBox-subsystem Tick/Draw split -- deferred to a
wave-60 follow-up per the team-lead scope ruling; documented as a
known FT=1 dialogue-timing desync, NOT a crash.

No new env var, no banner, no BOOT.md, no BANNERS change -- wave-59 is
a fix to the existing FIXED_TIMESTEP path, not a new lever.

FILES: src/game.cpp (_build_onscreen_objects_list helper + the
FT=1-gated call in game_tick_normal_state).
---
 src/game.cpp | 80 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 80 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/game.cpp b/src/game.cpp
index bd4966e..fe8eb87 100644
--- a/src/game.cpp
+++ b/src/game.cpp
@@ -580,6 +580,71 @@ void c------------------------------() {}
 */
 
 // standard in-game tick (as opposed to title-screen, inventory etc)
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0155, Phase 11 wave-59 -- FT=1 onscreen_objects
+// use-after-free fix). Rebuilds the visibility-culled onscreen_objects[]
+// list from the LIVE object list. This is the cull-ONLY half of
+// DrawScene's object-draw loop -- the same scr_x/scr_y onscreen test
+// and the same onscreen_objects[] / nOnscreenObjects / o->onscreen
+// writes -- with NO drawing and none of DrawScene's per-object render
+// bookkeeping (DamageText / shaketime / display_xoff). Drawcall-free:
+// it only READS sprite metadata (drawpoint / w / h), so it is safe to
+// run in the state half, which the FT=1 accumulator multi-runs.
+//
+// WHY: onscreen_objects[] is BUILT in DrawScene (the render half) and
+// READ + dereferenced by the player sim (PHandleSolidBrickObjects /
+// PHandleSolidMushyObjects, via HandlePlayer, in the state half). The
+// wave-57 accumulator runs the state half N times per render frame;
+// each game_tick_normal_state ends with Objects::CullDeleted() which
+// FREES deleted objects -- so on catch-up ticks 2..N HandlePlayer
+// dereferences freed pointers still in the un-rebuilt onscreen_objects[]
+// -> use-after-free / crash-to-DOS (exactly the CullDeleted comment
+// below: "blow up the program on the next tick"). Calling this at the
+// top of game_tick_normal_state under FT=1 rebuilds the list fresh
+// (live objects only) before every HandlePlayer. It also re-sets
+// o->onscreen per logic tick, closing the parallel AI-reads-stale-
+// o->onscreen desync (wave-59 sweep coupling 2).
+//
+// FT=0 NEVER calls this (the gate is in game_tick_normal_state) -- on
+// FT=0 DrawScene remains the sole builder and the legacy one-frame-
+// stale behavior is preserved byte-identically (wave-59 contract
+// sec.2.1).
+//
+// KEEP IN SYNC with DrawScene's object-loop cull test (the
+// MdsObjectLoopTimer loop) -- the scr_x/scr_y math + the 4-way bounds
+// check are duplicated here DELIBERATELY: DrawScene is the FT=0
+// byte-identity-critical path and is left 100% untouched.
+static void _build_onscreen_objects_list(void)
+{
+  Renderer *r      = Renderer::getInstance();
+  nOnscreenObjects = 0;
+
+  for (Object *o = lowestobject; o != NULL; o = o->higher)
+  {
+    if (o == player)
+      continue;  // player is handled specially, never in onscreen_objects
+
+    int scr_x = (o->x / CSFI) - (map.displayed_xscroll / CSFI);
+    int scr_y = (o->y / CSFI) - (map.displayed_yscroll / CSFI);
+    scr_x -= r->sprites.sprites[o->sprite].frame[o->frame].dir[o->dir].drawpoint.x;
+    scr_y -= r->sprites.sprites[o->sprite].frame[o->frame].dir[o->dir].drawpoint.y;
+
+    if (scr_x <= r->screenWidth && scr_y <= r->screenHeight + 26
+        && scr_x >= -r->sprites.sprites[o->sprite].w
+        && scr_y >= -r->sprites.sprites[o->sprite].h)
+    {
+      if (nOnscreenObjects < MAX_OBJECTS - 1)
+      {
+        onscreen_objects[nOnscreenObjects++] = o;
+        o->onscreen                          = true;
+      }
+    }
+    else
+    {
+      o->onscreen = false;
+    }
+  }
+}
+
 // DOS-PORT (patch 0152, Phase 11 wave-56 -- Track B B1): game_tick_-
 // normal() split at the W22A ModeSim / ModeDrawScene seam. Retained as
 // the 1:1 wrapper so the tickfunctions[] table entry stays valid; the
@@ -618,6 +683,21 @@ void game_tick_normal_state(void)
   // residual stays small).
   {
     NXE::Diag::ModeSimTimer _mst;
+
+    // patch 0155 (wave-59 -- FT=1 onscreen_objects use-after-free fix):
+    // under FIXED_TIMESTEP the accumulator multi-runs this state half N
+    // times per render frame. Rebuild the render-half-built
+    // onscreen_objects[] HERE, per logic tick, BEFORE HandlePlayer reads
+    // it (via PHandleSolidBrickObjects/MushyObjects) -- otherwise
+    // catch-up ticks 2..N dereference pointers a prior tick's
+    // CullDeleted freed. FT=1-GATED: on FT=0 DrawScene stays the sole
+    // builder and game_tick_normal_state is byte-identical to wave-58
+    // (the contract sec.2.1 non-negotiable). Placed inside the
+    // ModeSimTimer scope so the rebuild cost is honestly accounted as
+    // mode_sim.
+    if (fixed_timestep_active())
+      _build_onscreen_objects_list();
+
     Objects::UpdateBlockStates();
 
     if (!game.frozen)
